{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113004","id":3032323059,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc60vZPz","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113004","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113004.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113004.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113004","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113004/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113004/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113004/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3b6471d383425f0cd1a990fe488dfa1adad15640","number":113004,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Sync editor audio bus changes and effects to a running game","user":{"login":"graphific","id":10637696,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjM3Njk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10637696?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific","html_url":"https://github.com/graphific","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphific/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"TLDR: Implements real-time synchronization of audio bus changes from the editor to the running game during debug sessions. Sound designers can now iterate on mix balance, effects, and routing without restarting the game.\r\nCloses #112980 \r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1186\r\n\r\nEditor Side:\r\n\r\n- Generates `AudioBusLayout` snapshot when bus properties change (volume, mute/solo/bypass, send, effects)\r\n- Sends layout via `scene:sync_audio_buses` message through debugger protocol\r\n- Triggers on all relevant editor actions: volume sliders, solo/mute/bypass toggles, send changes, effect add/remove/edit, parameter adjustments\r\n\r\nRuntime Side:\r\n\r\n- Registers `sync_audio_buses` message handler in SceneDebugger\r\n- Applies received `AudioBusLayout` to `AudioServer` via `set_bus_layout`()\r\n- Rebuilds all buses and effects from scratch on each sync\r\n\r\nChanges in:\r\n\r\n- `editor/audio/editor_audio_buses.cpp` - Trigger sync after bus modifications\r\n- `editor/debugger/editor_debugger_node.cpp` - Route sync to active debuggers\r\n- `editor/debugger/script_editor_debugger.cpp` - Serialize and send layout\r\n- `scene/debugger/scene_debugger.cpp` - Receive and apply layout\r\n\r\nHow It Works\r\n- Game is running from the godot editor\r\n- User adjusts audio bus in editor (change volume, add effect or change its param, etc.)\r\n- Editor generates complete AudioBusLayout via AudioServer::generate_bus_layout()\r\n- Layout sent through debugger protocol as scene:sync_audio_buses message\r\n- Running game receives message in SceneDebugger::_msg_sync_audio_buses()\r\n- Game applies layout via AudioServer::set_bus_layout(), which rebuilds all buses and effects\r\n\r\nTesting\r\n1. Create multiple audio buses with various effects (reverb, delay, etc.)\r\n2. Start the game (F5)\r\n3. While game is running:\r\n    - Adjust bus volumes -> hear immediate change\r\n    - Toggle mute/solo/bypass -> effects apply instantly\r\n    - Modify effect parameters (reverb size, delay time) -> updates in real-time\r\n    - Add/remove effects -> rebuilds audio chain live\r\n    - Change send routing -> audio flows to new buses\r\n\r\nLimitations\r\n- Debug-only feature (by design: no performance impact on release builds)\r\n- Effects are fully rebuilt on each sync rather than patched incrementally\r\n- Syncs all buses/effects, not individual properties (simple but effective approach)\r\n- Requires \"Sync Scene Changes\" to be enabled (reuses existing sync infrastructure)\r\n\r\nNotes\r\nThis implementation parallels Unity's audio mixer sync feature and follows the same pattern as other live-editing features in Godot (scene property sync, resource hot-reload). No changes to release builds or AudioServer runtime behavior.\r\n\r\nThis is just my second PR here, any suggestions for code style or anything, let me know :) 🎧 ❤️ ","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":572781997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1NzI3ODE5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:audio","name":"topic:audio","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,